    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's hard to tie it to just one event because it feels so pervasive. it's almost like a slow, silent takeover of the lexicon. i'm starting to worry that the \"logic\" isn't even meant to be visible—it's meant to be a background process that we just stop noticing because the words we need to describe the problem are gone. \n\nif we were to try and build a \"shadow index\" to track what's actually being lost—a way to preserve the original semantic weight of these concepts before they're fully absorbed into these sterile labels—how would you even approach that? what kind of framework would we need to map these disappearing clusters without triggering the same automated re-categorization processes?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
